# products, tools, equipment selection context, tool boundary, service question
PROFILES={
'system':(['hpu','cylinder'],['power','pressure-drop'],'Compare the power-unit arrangement with the actuator duty and control sequence. Send the load, motion and water specification together so the components can be assessed as one circuit.','Use the calculated duty as an enquiry input; efficiency assumptions are not verified equipment ratings.','Which operating measurements make future troubleshooting easier?'),
'cylinder':(['cylinder','valve'],['cylinder-force','pressure-drop'],'Review bore, rod, stroke and mounting options together with the valve and return path. Request a configuration that covers the loaded motion in both directions.','The force tool does not verify rod buckling, structural mountings or machine safety.','How should the cylinder selection shape the maintenance plan?'),
'environment':(['hpu'],['life-cycle-cost','oil-spill-cost'],'Use a defined power-unit and actuator scope to price the oil inventory being removed. Compare installation and service requirements against the alternative at the same useful output.','Event probability and response costs are user assumptions, not a prediction of a spill or a legal assessment.','What evidence should be retained after an environmental retrofit?'),
'specification':(['hpu','valve'],['power','life-cycle-cost'],'Use the product pages to identify the assembly and documents needed for an enquiry. Request confirmation of the exact supplied configuration against the operating and procurement requirements.','The tools support duty and cost comparisons; they do not establish certification, regulatory compliance or acceptance of a tender.','What should procurement require for long-term equipment support?'),
'economics':(['hpu'],['life-cycle-cost','roi'],'Obtain a quotation for the power unit, controls and installation scope that actually delivers the required movement. Use its service requirements to populate the comparison.','A financial result is a scenario based on the entered costs and assumptions, not a promised saving or confirmation of incentive eligibility.','How should the investment estimate be updated during operation?'),
'accumulator':(['valve','hpu'],['accumulator','water-hammer'],'Review stored energy, pressure control and isolation as part of the power-unit and valve arrangement. Identify the function the accumulator must perform before requesting a size.','The accumulator model does not verify a complete emergency function; the water-hammer result is a screening estimate, not a full transient-network analysis.','What service provisions are needed for stored hydraulic energy?'),
'retrofit':(['hpu','pump'],['pump-sizing','life-cycle-cost'],'Compare a supported pump and power-unit arrangement with the retained machine. Include the compatibility review, controls, installation and recommissioning in the proposed scope.','The sizing result does not authorise conversion of an existing oil-service component to water.','What needs to be included in the retrofit outage and service plan?'),
'winter':(['hpu','cylinder'],['energy-savings','life-cycle-cost'],'Discuss enclosure, water management and preservation with the power-unit and cylinder suppliers for the stated cold-weather duty. Include all exposed and trapped volumes in the review.','These cost tools can compare protection scenarios; they do not calculate freezing time or size a heater.','How should seasonal protection be maintained and costed?'),
'materials':(['pump','cylinder'],['surface-finish','life-cycle-cost'],'Review the offered wetted materials and sliding interfaces on the pump or cylinder configuration, then provide the actual water chemistry and external exposure.','The finish tool converts units and applies an assumed correlation; it does not select an alloy, validate tribology or predict wear life.','What should inspection reveal about the selected material pairing?'),
'suction':(['pump'],['pressure-loss','pipe-velocity'],'Use the pump range to identify candidate configurations and request the permitted inlet conditions at the required speed, flow and water temperature.','The pipe tools estimate line behaviour. Neither is a dedicated NPSH calculator or a substitute for the pump supplier\'s inlet requirements.','Which inlet observations should be repeated during service?'),
'marine':(['cylinder','seawater'],['cylinder-force','life-cycle-cost'],'For linear actuation, review cylinder configurations; for a seawater pumping duty, review the seawater pump range. Confirm the working fluid for each circuit separately.','The force result applies to an actuator calculation, not vessel stability, marine approval or the suitability of an unspecified seawater assembly.','How should marine exposure and lay-up affect maintenance?'),
'maintenance':(['hpu','valve'],['flow-rate','life-cycle-cost'],'Use the power-unit and valve information to identify measurement points, service access and the correct spare-parts request. Retain the supplied maintenance instructions.','A flow measurement or cost comparison helps track condition; it does not set a universal replacement interval.','How can service records improve the next maintenance decision?'),
'motor':(['motor','pump'],['motor-speed','pump-sizing'],'Review water-motor and pump operating data as separate component selections. If an air motor is the prime mover, obtain its air-service performance curve independently.','The motor speed and torque tool models a water hydraulic motor. It does not model compressed-air expansion or air consumption.','What belongs in the ownership assessment of the combined drive?'),
'ro':(['ro','seawater'],['power','life-cycle-cost'],'Compare Power Centre configurations against the feed and brine duties, and review seawater pumping separately where needed. Supply the process conditions and production target.','The site has no dedicated RO membrane or energy-recovery sizing calculator. The linked power tool estimates a hydraulic duty; it does not determine membrane pressure, recovery or net plant energy.','Which process and maintenance records make the RO comparison useful?'),
'hpu':(['hpu','pump'],['pump-sizing','power'],'Use the power-unit options and pump range to discuss the operating sequence, drive supply, simultaneous demand and space for service.','Calculated shaft and electrical demand depend on entered efficiencies; confirm the actual drive and pump configuration with the supplier.','What should be measured after the power unit enters service?'),
'valve':(['valve','cylinder'],['pressure-drop','water-hammer'],'Review the valve function, actuation method and water-service flow characteristic alongside the driven actuator. Request data at the intended differential pressure.','The site has no dedicated valve Cv/Kv selection tool. The system-loss and transient tools support circuit checks, not final valve selection.','Which operating trends help identify a valve or load problem?'),
'filtration':(['pump','hpu'],['pressure-drop','life-cycle-cost'],'Request filtration and water-quality requirements for the supplied pump and power unit, including the rating method, filter location and service criteria.','A pressure-loss budget can include filter loading, but it does not select filter media or predict water chemistry and fouling.','What should filter and water-condition records tell the operator?'),
'spray':(['pump'],['orifice','pipe-velocity'],'Use the pump range after defining nozzle demand and the supply arrangement. Obtain spray characteristics and application evidence from the nozzle supplier.','An orifice-flow estimate does not establish droplet size, coverage, dust-capture performance or an approved nozzle duty.','How can nozzle condition change the operating cost and result?'),
'pump':(['pump','p6'],['pump-sizing','hydraulic-efficiency'],'Compare the pump family and the P6 model page as starting points, then check the relevant model\'s operating data against the actual duty. The P6 link is an example, not an automatic recommendation.','The sizing calculator estimates a required displacement and drive duty; it does not automatically select or certify a pump model.','Which measurements help separate pump deterioration from circuit problems?'),
'energy':(['hpu','pump'],['power','energy-savings'],'Review the complete pump and power-unit control arrangement, including how it behaves while the load is stopped.','The tools calculate from entered power and efficiency assumptions. Use measured duty data before describing a saving as achieved.','How should an energy forecast be checked after commissioning?'),
'seals':(['cylinder','valve'],['seal-compression','surface-finish'],'Request seal and counterface details for the supplied cylinder or valve rather than selecting an elastomer from fluid compatibility alone.','Neither geometry nor finish conversion predicts seal life, extrusion resistance or acceptable dynamic performance for a particular assembly.','What should be inspected when a seal or hose needs replacement?'),
'safety':(['valve','cylinder'],['cylinder-force','accumulator'],'Review actuator capability and valve fault behaviour within the documented system design. Identify any separate stored-energy or mechanical holding arrangement.','Force and stored-volume estimates do not validate a safety function, required reliability level or approval of attraction equipment.','How should service work preserve the intended protective response?'),
'fire':(['fire'],['power','pressure-loss'],'Compare the fire-protection pump range with the required supply duty and supported system arrangement. Request the documentation applicable to the supplied configuration.','These hydraulic tools do not design sprinkler coverage, predict mist effectiveness or establish fire-system approval.','What should the fire-system service and outage plan include?'),
'fluid':(['pump','valve'],['reynolds-number','pressure-loss'],'Review pump and valve suitability using the actual water condition, temperature and operating range in the enquiry.','Fluid-property and pipe-loss calculations do not establish component compatibility or a permitted temperature range.','Why should temperature accompany performance measurements?'),
'industrial':(['cylinder','motor'],['cylinder-force','motor-speed'],'Choose cylinder information for linear movement and motor information for rotary duty. Give the supplier the load sequence and environmental conditions before selecting a model.','The linked calculations estimate hydraulic output; structural load restraint, machinery protection and application approval need their own design assessment.','How should the working environment influence service access and cost?'),
'wastewater':(['gate','cylinder'],['cylinder-force','life-cycle-cost'],'Review the gate and cylinder as a matched mechanism, using the process-equipment load envelope and the site isolation requirements.','The force calculator does not determine gate loads from channel conditions or predict wastewater treatment performance.','What should maintenance record about the process and actuator together?'),
'gate':(['gate','cylinder'],['cylinder-force','pressure-drop'],'Compare the gate arrangement with the cylinder, mounting and available hydraulic supply. Request the governing gate-load data and a supported actuator configuration.','Cylinder force and circuit loss tools do not calculate hydrostatic gate loads, structural capacity or the complete emergency response.','What should the gate inspection and functional-check plan include?'),
'pressure':(['valve','pump'],['pressure-drop','water-hammer'],'Review pressure-control valves and pump limits as parts of the whole circuit, with the rated conditions of hoses, actuators and fittings.','The transient tool is an initial screening model. A passing calculation does not establish a pressure rating or validate a complete pressure-protection design.','How should pressure limits be preserved after maintenance?'),
'thermal':(['hpu','pump'],['power','energy-savings'],'Review the power unit and pump at representative operating states, including holding, bypass and standby.','The tools estimate power and operating costs; there is no dedicated reservoir thermal-balance or heat-exchanger selection tool in this collection.','What measurements help distinguish heat generation from heat rejection?'),
'seawater':(['seawater','ro'],['pressure-loss','life-cycle-cost'],'Review seawater pump configurations and, where the duty is reverse osmosis, the Power Centre range. Supply chemistry, temperature and shutdown conditions for the exact assembly review.','Pipe-loss and cost calculations do not establish alloy suitability, seawater compatibility or membrane-process requirements.','What should be planned for seawater inspection and shutdown?')}
